## The brief
Tizer & Tide is a privately owned static caravan on Sandringham Rise at Pendine Sands Holiday Park in Carmarthenshire. It sleeps up to eight and is run by a newly established family business.

The owners wanted guests to book directly rather than relying only on third-party listing sites. That meant a website that shows the caravan off, answers guests' questions before they ask them, and lets them check dates and pay online in one go.

## A seaside look
The design takes its colours from the Tizer & Tide logo: deep navy and a warm sunset orange, with palm-leaf shapes sweeping behind the content. Condensed uppercase headings and rounded orange buttons keep it bright and holiday-like, while the owners' own photos of the caravan and Pendine beach do the selling.

## Book direct, pay online
The Availability & Booking page has a live calendar showing available and booked dates month by month. Guests pick their start and end dates, add their details and the number of adults and children, and see the total before paying securely online by debit or credit card.

Calls to check availability sit in the header, on every page and in the footer, so the booking page is always one click away.

## Everything a guest wants to know
- **Our Caravan** covers the key facts up front (sleeps 8, pet-free, 3, 4 and 7-night stays) and then walks through the bedrooms, kitchen, living area, Starlink Wi-Fi, smart TVs, heating, cot and high chair, parking and the park's facilities, with a downloadable park map.
- **Gallery** shows the caravan inside and out and the beach on the doorstep.
- **Local Area** is a guide to Pendine's seven-mile beach, the Museum of Land Speed, nearby seaside towns like Tenby, Saundersfoot and Laugharne, family days out and places to eat.
- **Events** lists the racing and motorsport held on Pendine Sands through the year.
- **FAQs** answer questions about booking, payment, pets and arrival times, alongside clear terms and conditions.

## Under the hood
The website is built in WordPress with Bricks, with a booking calendar and online checkout. Layouts adapt across desktop, tablet and mobile, which matters for a site most holidaymakers will browse on their phones.

NC Digital also hosts the website for Tizer & Tide.

